# Append-only evidence CSVs: two concurrent workflow runs (a capture and a
# poll) each append their own rows to the same file. A default 3-way merge
# treats "both sides added different lines at EOF" as a conflict and the
# rebase in commit_evidence.sh dies. `merge=union` is a git built-in that
# keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of conflicting -- exactly right for an
# append-only log. commit_evidence.sh then de-duplicates and re-sorts.
localdata/*.csv merge=union
